              "id": "CVE-2026-43827",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "apache-shiro: Apache Shiro: Session fixation vulnerability due to improper session invalidation upon login"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Default configurations of Apache Shiro have a session fixation vulnerability.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Shiro from 1.0 to 2.1.0, and 3.0.0-alpha-1.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.1.1, or 3.0.0-alpha-2 or later, which fixes the issue.\n\nIn the affected versions, when a session already exists, it is not invalidated upon successful login, nor is a new session being generated with a new ID."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43827",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43827\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: org.apache.shiro:shiro-core\nFixed Version: 2.2.0, 3.0.0-alpha-2\nLink: [CVE-2026-43827](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43827)\nDefault configurations of Apache Shiro have a session fixation vulnerability.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Shiro from 1.0 to 2.1.0, and 3.0.0-alpha-1.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.1.1, or 3.0.0-alpha-2 or later, which fixes the issue.\n\nIn the affected versions, when a session already exists, it is not invalidated upon successful login, nor is a new session being generated with a new ID.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43827**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|org.apache.shiro:shiro-core|2.2.0, 3.0.0-alpha-2|[CVE-2026-43827](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43827)|\n\nDefault configurations of Apache Shiro have a session fixation vulnerability.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Shiro from 1.0 to 2.1.0, and 3.0.0-alpha-1.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.1.1, or 3.0.0-alpha-2 or later, which fixes the issue.\n\nIn the affected versions, when a session already exists, it is not invalidated upon successful login, nor is a new session being generated with a new ID."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:N/SA:N/RE:L/U:Amber",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
